    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="d208-04" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve05p1/d208-04"/>

                <head>209. Airgram A–22 From the Department of State to
                    the Embassy in Nigeria<anchor n="1" xml:id="d209-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d209-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1971-06-21T16:11:00-05:00">June 22, 1971, 4:11 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <pb facs="d209-01" n="1" xml:id="d209-01"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>Policy Planning Paper</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>REF</label>
                    <item>CA–5632, November 3, 1970</item>
                </list>
                <p>Attached are three copies of the Policy Planning Paper for Nigeria, as approved
                    by the members of the NSC Interdepartmental
                    Group for Africa.</p>
                <p>The paper constitutes an official statement of US policy towards Nigeria and
                    should be used as a guideline by all elements of the Embassy in the preparation
                    of policy statements, action plans and future budgetary projections.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Rogers</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d209-a1.xml" xpointer="d209-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d209-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d209-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1970–73, POL 1 Nigeria-U.S. Secret; Limdis; Noforn. Drafted by Rawls on June
                    21. The annexes are not published.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d209-f2" n="2" xml:id="d209-f2-content">
                <p>The Policy Planning Paper for Nigeria, dated June 1971 and approved by the
                    National Security Council Inter-departmental Group for Africa, contained
                    sections on U.S. interests, U.S. objectives, Nigeriaʼs objectives, and
                    recommended courses of action.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
